Rather than pulling `onChange` out, spread the props first and put the props the connector owns after the spread, the way `ProxySelectInputConnector` does. That also stops a parent's `isDisabled` from hiding `isFetching`, and a parent's `values`/`value` from overriding the connector's. Same change in `MetadataProfileSelectInputConnector` (keep `value={value ?? ''}` there), and add `isDisabled: PropTypes.bool` to both propTypes:
```jsx
<SelectInput
  {...this.props}
  values={this.getSelectValues()}
  onChange={this.onChange}
  isDisabled={this.props.isDisabled || isFetching}
/>
```

